  "answer_core": "Option 3 can work, but only if you verify the support and resources before you commit. First, ask your advisor directly whether he backs the cross‑lab direction, whether funding covers the work, and whether he is comfortable with a real co‑advisor arrangement. If that is positive, speak with the single‑cell postdoc about what data access, authorship expectations, and PI approval would look like. Move forward only after you have a clear yes on data and funding. If the collaboration is solid, pursue the project; if not, fall back to the more standard tumor‑evolution path in your home lab. Set an internal checkpoint around 18 months: if you do not have a publishable result by then, pivot while you still have time.",
